{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778521464135,"sessionID":"ses_1e7eef306ffe0Uf6QZyw5f2na3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8527fffcc5bbc0cc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -i \"skeletal\" src/ontology/cl-edit.owl | head -n 50","description":"Search for \"skeletal\" case-insensitively in cl-edit.owl and show first 50 lines"},"output":"# Class: obo:CL_0000188 (cell of skeletal muscle)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000188 \"A somatic cell located in skeletal muscle.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000188 \"skeletal muscle cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000188 \"cell of skeletal muscle\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000355 (multi-potent skeletal muscle stem cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18282570\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000355 \"A multifate stem cell found in skeletal muscle than can differentiate into many different cell types, including muscle. Distinct cell type from satellite cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000355 \"multi-potent skeletal muscle stem cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000515 (skeletal muscle myoblast)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000515 \"A myoblast that differentiates into skeletal muscle fibers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000515 \"skeletal myoblast\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000515 \"skeletal muscle myoblast\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000594 (skeletal muscle satellite cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000594 \"Skeletal muscle satellite cells are not traditionally referred to as myoblasts.  They are a heterogeneous population whose division, following activiation, contributes to the formation of skeletal muscle fibers and to maintenance of the skeletal muscle statelite cell population.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000594 \"skeletal muscle satellite cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35179487\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000743 \"Despite historical descriptions as 'terminally differentiated,' hypertrophic chondrocytes survive and transdifferentiate into osteoblasts. Genetic lineage tracing shows that hypertrophic chondrocytes do not simply undergo apoptosis but cross the cartilage–bone boundary, dedifferentiate into skeletal stem/progenitor cells, and then redifferentiate into osteoblasts and osteocytes. Single-cell RNA-seq further indicates that these chondrocyte-derived SSPCs are a major source of trabecular osteoblasts and marrow adipocytes.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:mtg_cardiacconduct_nov11\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0323052908\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22426062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:4711263\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000746 \"Cardiac muscle cells are striated muscle cells that are responsible for heart contraction. In mammals, the contractile fiber resembles those of skeletal muscle but are only one third as large in diameter, are richer in sarcoplasm, and contain centrally located instead of peripheral nuclei.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000857 \"A skeletal muscle myoblast that differentiates into slow muscle fibers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000858 \"A skeletal muscle myoblast that differentiates into fast muscle fibers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skeletal_muscle\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002215 \"A type II muscle cell that contains a low content of myoglobin, relatively few mitochondria, relatively few blood capillaries and large amounts of glycogen. Type II B fibres are white, geared to generate ATP by anaerobic metabolic processes, not able to supply skeletal muscle fibres continuously with sufficient ATP, fatigue easily, split ATP at a fast rate and have a fast contraction velocity.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18353863\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22043022\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22476723\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33193034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002669 \"A spiral ligament fibrocyte that is located in the deepest part of the inferior spiral ligament, directly lining the bony otic capsule. Distinguished from ion-transporting Type I and II fibrocytes, it utilises actin-myosin stress fibres and anchoring interactions to regulate basilar membrane tension. It has an elongated morphology, is most numerous in the basal, high-frequency cochlea, and expresses contractile and cytoskeletal proteins in mice, including α‑smooth muscle actin, non‑muscle myosin II, caldesmon, and the water channel Aquaporin‑1(Mahendrasingam et al., 2011; Kelly et al., 2012).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18816858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002673 \"A skeletal muscle cell that is part of the tongue.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ZFIN:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005024 \"A motor neuron that innervates a skeletal muscle.  These motor neurons are all excitatory and cholinergic.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0007001 \"Cell that has the potential to form a skeletal cell type (e.g. cells in periosteum, cells in marrow) and produce extracellular matrix (often mineralized) and skeletal tissue (often mineralized).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0007001 \"Needs logical definition. Should be capable_of skeletal system morphogenesis? or skeletal tissue development? needs to be added to GO. NOTES:a cell type of the early embryo (see also: mesenchymal cells) that will give rise to mineralized connective tissue. Scleroblasts can differentiate into osteoblasts (bone-forming cells), chondroblasts (cartilage-forming cells), odontoblasts (dentin-forming cells), ameloblasts (enamel-forming cells). The mesenchymal cells developing into osteoblasts and chondroblasts are derived from the mesoderm. Those developing into odontoblasts are neural crest cells. Those developing into ameloblasts are derived from the ectoderm. (http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=scleroblasts)\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008002 (skeletal muscle fiber)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0323052908\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008002 \"A transversely striated, synctial cell of skeletal muscle. It is formed when proliferating myoblasts exit the cell cycle, differentiate and fuse.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008002 \"skeletal muscle fiber\"@en)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14699587\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008010 \"A cranial motor neuron whose soma is located in the midbrain andor hindbrain and which innervates the skeletal muscles of the eye or tongue.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008011 (skeletal muscle satellite stem cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008011 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that divides by stem cell division.  A proportion of this population undergoes symmetric stem cell division, producing two skeletal muscle satellite stem cells. The rest undergo asymmetric stem cell division - retaining their identity while budding off a daughter cell that differentiates into an adult skeletal muscle myoblast.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008011 \"skeletal muscle satellite stem cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008012 (quiescent skeletal muscle satellite cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008012 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that is mitotically quiescent.  These cells are wedge shaped and have a large nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio with few organelles, a small nucleus and condensed interphase chromatin. Satellite cells typically remain in this state until activated following muscle damage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008012 \"quiescent skeletal muscle satellite cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008016 (activated skeletal muscle satellite cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008016 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that has become mitotically active - typically following muscle damage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008016 \"activated skeletal muscle satellite cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008017 (adult skeletal muscle myoblast)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008017 \"A skeletal muscle myoblast that is part of a skeletal mucle.  These cells are formed following acivation and division of skeletal muscle satellite cells. They form a transient population that is lost when they fuse to form skeletal muscle fibers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0008017 \"The vast majority of these cells develop from skeletal muscle satellite cells, although there are some reports of other origins.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008017 \"adult skeletal muscle myoblast\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008020 (skeletal muscle satellite myogenic cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dos\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008020 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that undergoes symmetric division to produce two adult skeleltal muscle myoblasts.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008020 \"skeletal muscle satellite myogenic cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1016/B978-0-12-801238-3.05364-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Alpha_motor_neuron&oldid=957148643\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008038 \"A large, multipolar lower motor neuron of the brainstem and spinal cord that innervates the extrafusal muscle fibers of skeletal muscle and are directly responsible for initiating their contraction. While their cell bodies are in the CNS (in the anterior gray horn of the spinal cord), they are part of the somatic nervous system - a branch of the PNS.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Lower_motor_neuron&oldid=952547294\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008039 \"The motor neurons of vertebrates that directly innervate skeletal muscles. They receive input from upper motor neurons.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1016/B978-0-443-10321-6.00004-7\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Extrafusal_muscle_fiber&oldid=978415293\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008046 \"A skeletal muscle fiber that is innervated by alpha motor neuron and generates tension by contracting, thereby allowing for skeletal movement. These fibers make up the large mass of skeletal muscle tissue and are attached to bones by tendons.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1016/B978-0-443-10321-6.00004-7\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Intrafusal_muscle_fiber&oldid=937508784\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008047 \"A skeletal muscle fiber that is part of a muscle spindle. These are specialized muscle fibers that serve as proprioceptors, detecting the amount and rate of change in length of a muscle. They are innervated by both sensory neurons and motor neurons (gamma and beta motorneurons, collectively referred to as fusimotor neurons).\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0009097 (embryonic skeletal muscle fiber)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32094117\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7196501\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009097 \"A skeletal muscle fiber found in an embryo. In mammalian embryos, skeletal muscle expresses myosin heavy chain-embryonic (MyHC-emb, encoded by the MYH3 gene), which regulates skeletal muscle development.\")\n","metadata":{"output":"# Class: obo:CL_0000188 (cell of skeletal muscle)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000188 \"A somatic cell located in skeletal muscle.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000188 \"skeletal muscle cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000188 \"cell of skeletal muscle\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000355 (multi-potent skeletal muscle stem cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18282570\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000355 \"A multifate stem cell found in skeletal muscle than can differentiate into many different cell types, including muscle. Distinct cell type from satellite cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000355 \"multi-potent skeletal muscle stem cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000515 (skeletal muscle myoblast)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000515 \"A myoblast that differentiates into skeletal muscle fibers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000515 \"skeletal myoblast\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000515 \"skeletal muscle myoblast\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000594 (skeletal muscle satellite cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000594 \"Skeletal muscle satellite cells are not traditionally referred to as myoblasts.  They are a heterogeneous population whose division, following activiation, contributes to the formation of skeletal muscle fibers and to maintenance of the skeletal muscle statelite cell population.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000594 \"skeletal muscle satellite cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35179487\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000743 \"Despite historical descriptions as 'terminally differentiated,' hypertrophic chondrocytes survive and transdifferentiate into osteoblasts. Genetic lineage tracing shows that hypertrophic chondrocytes do not simply undergo apoptosis but cross the cartilage–bone boundary, dedifferentiate into skeletal stem/progenitor cells, and then redifferentiate into osteoblasts and osteocytes. Single-cell RNA-seq further indicates that these chondrocyte-derived SSPCs are a major source of trabecular osteoblasts and marrow adipocytes.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:mtg_cardiacconduct_nov11\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0323052908\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22426062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:4711263\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000746 \"Cardiac muscle cells are striated muscle cells that are responsible for heart contraction. In mammals, the contractile fiber resembles those of skeletal muscle but are only one third as large in diameter, are richer in sarcoplasm, and contain centrally located instead of peripheral nuclei.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000857 \"A skeletal muscle myoblast that differentiates into slow muscle fibers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000858 \"A skeletal muscle myoblast that differentiates into fast muscle fibers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skeletal_muscle\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002215 \"A type II muscle cell that contains a low content of myoglobin, relatively few mitochondria, relatively few blood capillaries and large amounts of glycogen. Type II B fibres are white, geared to generate ATP by anaerobic metabolic processes, not able to supply skeletal muscle fibres continuously with sufficient ATP, fatigue easily, split ATP at a fast rate and have a fast contraction velocity.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18353863\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22043022\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22476723\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33193034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002669 \"A spiral ligament fibrocyte that is located in the deepest part of the inferior spiral ligament, directly lining the bony otic capsule. Distinguished from ion-transporting Type I and II fibrocytes, it utilises actin-myosin stress fibres and anchoring interactions to regulate basilar membrane tension. It has an elongated morphology, is most numerous in the basal, high-frequency cochlea, and expresses contractile and cytoskeletal proteins in mice, including α‑smooth muscle actin, non‑muscle myosin II, caldesmon, and the water channel Aquaporin‑1(Mahendrasingam et al., 2011; Kelly et al., 2012).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18816858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002673 \"A skeletal muscle cell that is part of the tongue.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ZFIN:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005024 \"A motor neuron that innervates a skeletal muscle.  These motor neurons are all excitatory and cholinergic.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0007001 \"Cell that has the potential to form a skeletal cell type (e.g. cells in periosteum, cells in marrow) and produce extracellular matrix (often mineralized) and skeletal tissue (often mineralized).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0007001 \"Needs logical definition. Should be capable_of skeletal system morphogenesis? or skeletal tissue development? needs to be added to GO. NOTES:a cell type of the early embryo (see also: mesenchymal cells) that will give rise to mineralized connective tissue. Scleroblasts can differentiate into osteoblasts (bone-forming cells), chondroblasts (cartilage-forming cells), odontoblasts (dentin-forming cells), ameloblasts (enamel-forming cells). The mesenchymal cells developing into osteoblasts and chondroblasts are derived from the mesoderm. Those developing into odontoblasts are neural crest cells. Those developing into ameloblasts are derived from the ectoderm. (http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=scleroblasts)\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008002 (skeletal muscle fiber)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0323052908\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008002 \"A transversely striated, synctial cell of skeletal muscle. It is formed when proliferating myoblasts exit the cell cycle, differentiate and fuse.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008002 \"skeletal muscle fiber\"@en)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14699587\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008010 \"A cranial motor neuron whose soma is located in the midbrain andor hindbrain and which innervates the skeletal muscles of the eye or tongue.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008011 (skeletal muscle satellite stem cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008011 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that divides by stem cell division.  A proportion of this population undergoes symmetric stem cell division, producing two skeletal muscle satellite stem cells. The rest undergo asymmetric stem cell division - retaining their identity while budding off a daughter cell that differentiates into an adult skeletal muscle myoblast.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008011 \"skeletal muscle satellite stem cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008012 (quiescent skeletal muscle satellite cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008012 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that is mitotically quiescent.  These cells are wedge shaped and have a large nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio with few organelles, a small nucleus and condensed interphase chromatin. Satellite cells typically remain in this state until activated following muscle damage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008012 \"quiescent skeletal muscle satellite cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008016 (activated skeletal muscle satellite cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008016 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that has become mitotically active - typically following muscle damage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008016 \"activated skeletal muscle satellite cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008017 (adult skeletal muscle myoblast)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008017 \"A skeletal muscle myoblast that is part of a skeletal mucle.  These cells are formed following acivation and division of skeletal muscle satellite cells. They form a transient population that is lost when they fuse to form skeletal muscle fibers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0008017 \"The vast majority of these cells develop from skeletal muscle satellite cells, although there are some reports of other origins.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008017 \"adult skeletal muscle myoblast\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0008020 (skeletal muscle satellite myogenic cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dos\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008020 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that undergoes symmetric division to produce two adult skeleltal muscle myoblasts.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008020 \"skeletal muscle satellite myogenic cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1016/B978-0-12-801238-3.05364-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Alpha_motor_neuron&oldid=957148643\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008038 \"A large, multipolar lower motor neuron of the brainstem and spinal cord that innervates the extrafusal muscle fibers of skeletal muscle and are directly responsible for initiating their contraction. While their cell bodies are in the CNS (in the anterior gray horn of the spinal cord), they are part of the somatic nervous system - a branch of the PNS.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Lower_motor_neuron&oldid=952547294\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008039 \"The motor neurons of vertebrates that directly innervate skeletal muscles. They receive input from upper motor neurons.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1016/B978-0-443-10321-6.00004-7\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Extrafusal_muscle_fiber&oldid=978415293\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008046 \"A skeletal muscle fiber that is innervated by alpha motor neuron and generates tension by contracting, thereby allowing for skeletal movement. These fibers make up the large mass of skeletal muscle tissue and are attached to bones by tendons.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1016/B978-0-443-10321-6.00004-7\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Intrafusal_muscle_fiber&oldid=937508784\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008047 \"A skeletal muscle fiber that is part of a muscle spindle. These are specialized muscle fibers that serve as proprioceptors, detecting the amount and rate of change in length of a muscle. They are innervated by both sensory neurons and motor neurons (gamma and beta motorneurons, collectively referred to as fusimotor neurons).\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0009097 (embryonic skeletal muscle fiber)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32094117\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7196501\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009097 \"A skeletal muscle fiber found in an embryo. In mammalian embryos, skeletal muscle expresses myosin heavy chain-embryonic (MyHC-emb, encoded by the MYH3 gene), which regulates skeletal muscle development.\")\n","exit":0,"description":"Search for \"skeletal\" case-insensitively in cl-edit.owl and show first 50 lines","truncated":false},"title":"Search for \"skeletal\" case-insensitively in cl-edit.owl and show first 50 lines","time":{"start":1778521464129,"end":1778521464133}},"id":"prt_e1823ab2c00172u5McDIgCDRJX","sessionID":"ses_1e7eef306ffe0Uf6QZyw5f2na3","messageID":"msg_e18229fed001X4Z0QDQeuN5rSW"}}
